Jonas shows me my desk.
"Here is your desk, Maya," Jonas says.
I stand in front of the desk.
I have a desk and a chair.
"The desk is big," I say.
Jonas asks, "Do you have your laptop?"
"Yes, I have my laptop," I answer.
I put the laptop on the desk.
Jonas looks at the desk.
"But you don't have a monitor," he says.
"That's right," I say.
"I need two monitors."
Jonas laughs.
"Okay, two monitors," Jonas says.
"Do you need a keyboard?" he asks.
"Yes, I don't have a keyboard," I answer.
"And I need a mouse too."
Jonas counts: "So, two monitors, one keyboard, and one mouse."
"I am ordering the things now," he says.
"Thank you very much, Jonas," I say happily.
